task: json-decode-threshold-trampoline
agent: opus-depth
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/json-decode-threshold-trampoline
worktree: ../okay-wt-json-trampoline
spec: specs/iterative-recursive-decode.md (root 2 of 2: Json.decode)

why: root 1 (Cbor.get, cbor-decode-threshold-trampoline, landed
  3eb30c0a) proved the design and the JMH gate (3 forks, not 1 —
  a single-fork run there showed a false 53% regression). This lane
  is the second and last root: `Json.decode`.

  Different from Cbor.get in one structural way: Json.decode has no
  mutable reader object to hang a depth counter on (Cbor.In does) —
  Json.decode is a pure function of (Schema, Json). Depth is threaded
  as an explicit parameter through new private helpers
  (`decodeAt`/`decodeNative`), not read off shared state. And
  Json.decode does not need to ENFORCE Codecs.maxDepth itself — that
  refusal already happens upstream, at the parse/projection layer
  (Json.isCut cuts a too-deep document before decode ever sees it).
  This lane adds ONLY the native/trampoline stack-safety switch, so
  Json.decode becomes safe on ANY input depth, not only ones that
  came through Json.parse's own cut.

what: `Json.decode`'s public signature is unchanged. Internally: split
  into `decodeAt` (checks depth, dispatches) / `decodeNative` (today's
  body, renamed, recursive calls threaded with `depth+1`) /
  `decodeC` + `fieldC` (the Cont-based trampoline past
  NativeThreshold, mirroring Cbor.get's getC/fieldC exactly). Zero
  casts, same technique as root 1 (Cont's invariance needs one .map
  at the same two erasure points `decode` already widens for free via
  Either's covariance).

predict: no regression on the common (shallow) case — gated by a
  3-fork JMH run on `compare/CodecBenchmark`'s existing JSON decode
  benchmarks (encodeSumInterp/decodeSumInterpAst or equivalent),
  learning from root 1's false alarm. Once this lands, both roots of
  iterative-recursive-decode.md are closed and Codecs.maxDepth /
  TestVector's stress depth become a SEPARATE follow-up decision, not
  assumed here.
